# Document Lifecycle

Document lifecycle means everything that can happen to a document inside the app.

A real RAG app should not only upload and ask questions.

It should manage documents from beginning to end.

## Main Lifecycle Steps

```text
1. Upload
2. Validate
3. Store
4. Index
5. Use in chat
6. Re-index
7. Delete
8. Version
9. Rename
10. Share
11. View details and activity
```

## 1. Upload

The user uploads a file.

Example:

```text
company-x-branch-morocco.pdf
```

## 2. Validate

The backend checks:

```text
Is it a PDF, TXT, or Markdown file?
Is the file size allowed?
Is the file safe?
```

## 3. Store

The backend stores the original file and creates a database record.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "doc_001",
  fileName: "company-x-branch-morocco.pdf",
  originalName: "company-x-branch-morocco.pdf",
  storedPath: "uploads/...",
  status: "uploaded"
}
```

## 4. Index

The document is:

```text
loaded
split into chunks
embedded
stored in vector database
```

Then status becomes:

```text
indexed
```

## 5. Use In Chat

The document can now be searched by the chatbot.

Example:

```text
Who manages MA-OPS?
```

## 6. Re-index

If the file changes, the old chunks should be replaced.

Example:

```text
Morocco branch PDF version 1 is replaced by version 2.
Old chunks are deleted.
New chunks are created.
```

## 7. Delete

When a document is deleted, we should delete:

```text
file record
stored file
chunks
embeddings
related index data
```

## 8. Version

Versioning means keeping history.

Example:

```text
morocco-policy-v1.pdf
morocco-policy-v2.pdf
```

This helps answer:

```text
Which document version was used?
```

## 9. Rename

The owner/admin can rename a document.

The app updates:

```text
document display name
source label used in answers
renamedAt timestamp
activity log
```

## 10. Share

The owner/admin can share a document as:

```text
private
team
public
```

Team sharing requires selecting a team the user belongs to.

## 11. Details And Activity

The frontend now has a document details panel.

It shows:

```text
display name
version
access level
chunk count
source type
version history
document activity timeline
```

Activity examples:

```text
document indexed
document renamed
document shared
document re-indexed
document deleted
```

## Simple Presentation Version

```text
Document lifecycle manages files from upload to indexing, sharing, renaming, re-indexing, deletion, versioning, and activity history. This makes the RAG app easier to control and trust.
```
